WEBVTT

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.030
from a lot of perspectives.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:31.997
Some of those reforms have been good.

00:00:31.997 --> 00:00:34.263
Some of them have been not so good.

00:00:34.263 --> 00:00:36.463
And we know why kids drop out.

00:00:36.463 --> 00:00:37.930
We know why kids don't learn.

00:00:37.963 --> 00:00:40.863
It's either poverty, low attendance,

00:00:40.863 --> 00:00:43.230
negative peer influences...

00:00:43.263 --> 00:00:44.863
We know why.

00:00:44.897 --> 00:00:47.197
But one of the things
that we never discuss

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.530
or we rarely discuss

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:53.797
is the value and importance
of human connection.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.030
Relationships.

00:00:56.063 --> 00:00:59.663
James Comer says
that no significant learning

00:00:59.663 --> 00:01:02.130
can occur without
a significant relationship.